course: dictionary
lesson: 5839
title: Words ending in -er
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A maker is someone or something that makes things. The ending -er often shows the one who does the action: teach becomes teacher, bake becomes baker, and make becomes maker.
explain: Maker can mean a person, a company or a machine. «Car makers in Sweden test cars with a sharp swerve» means companies that build cars. A coffee maker is a machine that makes coffee.
explain: A maker can also be a person who likes building and inventing things. To check the meaning, swap in "the one who makes" and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Maker means a person, company or machine that makes something.
fact: A maker can also be a person who likes building and inventing things.
fact: «Makers» is the plural, so it means more than one maker.
fact: Phrases with maker include toy maker, cake maker, peacemaker, troublemaker and decision maker.
fact: Many words ending in -er name someone or something that does an action, like teacher, baker and maker.
exercise: «Car makers in Sweden test cars with a sharp swerve.» Who are the car makers? | *Companies that build cars | Drivers who race in Sweden | Teachers of car driving | People who sell petrol
exercise: «Many medicines are naturally bitter, so makers add sweet flavours for children.» Who are the makers here? | *Companies that make medicines | Bitter fruits | Teachers who give children lessons | Children who like sweets
exercise: Ella's dad says she is a maker because she builds model bridges from cardboard. What does maker mean here? | A rule for examiners | A troublemaker at school | *A person who likes building and inventing things | A machine that makes coffee
test: «Acid makes milk proteins clump; cheese-makers use this to make soft cheese.» What is a cheese-maker? | Machine that cuts bread | *A person who makes cheese | Shop that sells cheese | Cow that gives milk
test: What is a peacemaker? | A toy maker who makes teddy bears | A machine that makes peace signs | Someone who starts fights | *Someone who helps stop fights and bring peace
exam: In the sentence «The bread maker makes a loaf every hour», what does maker mean? | A baker who sings all day | *A machine that makes bread | A child who eats bread every hour | A shop that sells bread
